[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="FirstMvpSkillData" load_steps=2 format=3]

; Riftwrought — Gate 1E: Emberbolt, the spell Foundation Skill (D-219).
;
; Canonical foundation (design/SKILLS_AND_SKILL_MODIFICATION.md):
;   "Fire Projectile Spell" — Spell, Projectile, Hit, Fire.
;   "Emberbolt is a direct Fire Projectile Spell using the shared one-handed
;    cast family."
;   "Emberbolt provides an understandable conventional Spell against which Void
;    behavior remains visibly unusual."
;
; THE ONE THING THAT MAKES IT A SPELL RATHER THAN AN ATTACK: its damage is
; SKILL-DEFINED, not weapon-derived. damage_source = SPELL and spell_damage =
; 130.0, so the Cantor Wand's own Physical weapon damage is irrelevant to what
; Emberbolt deals. That is the readable contrast the canon asks for, and it is
; a property of this record rather than a branch in the code.
;
; 130 Fire against the reused 300-Life Graveblade is ceil(300 / 130) = 3 Hits,
; deliberately one more than the Watchsteel Sword's two: a Spell that ignored
; the weapon should not also out-damage it at the same Level.
;
; FIRE WITHOUT IGNITE. The brief: "Do NOT implement Ignite, Chain, Return,
; impact-area Augments, transformations, or additional projectiles yet."
; Emberbolt therefore deals Fire damage and nothing else — no ailment, no
; burning ground, no secondary. The first MVP has no Fire Resistance either, so
; final = raw exactly as every other Hit in the project.
;
; Range 10.50 m, inside the 13.532 m the accepted camera shows ahead of the
; body; 22.0 m/s gives a 0.48 s flight, slightly slower and heavier-reading
; than Splinter Shot's arrow.

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/skills/first_mvp_skill_data.gd" id="1_skill"]

